   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 50 of the laws of 2021, enacting the state operations\nbudget, in relation to services and expenses relating to investigations and\nhearings",
    "basePrintNo": "S7195",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7195-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 50 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Appropriations",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7195\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 50 of the laws of 2021, enacting the state oper-\nations budget, in relation to services and expenses relating to investi-\ngations and hearings\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow for state reimbursement of costs associated with a constitu-\ntional inquiry.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one allows for appropriations included in the recently enacted\nbudget to also support the necessary costs of investigations, hearings\nand proceedings prescribed under article 6, section 24 of the New York\nState Constitution and articles 7-c and 13-a of the Judiciary Law.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCosts incurred under the constitutional and statutory provisions cited\nabove are rare, unexpected and extraordinary in nature, and a mechanism\nfor payment of such expenses was not included in the enacted budget.\nThis bill would ensure that expenses pertaining to all matters of a\nconstitutional inquiry are provided for in full.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nExpenditures would be supported under existing appropriations.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
